#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:100
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Context Browser is a tabbed browser that provides many different kinds of "
"information about the currently playing track, and your music collection in "
"general."
msgstr "ព័ត៌មាន​ បទ​ ដន្ត្រី​."

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:103
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "The Home Tab"
msgstr "ផ្ទះ"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:105
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Home</guilabel> Tab offers information about your entire music "
"collection. In this tab you will find the <guilabel>"
"Your Favorite Tracks</guilabel>, <guilabel>Your Newest Tracks</guilabel>"
", and <guilabel>Least Listened Songs</guilabel> panes."
msgstr ""
"<guilabel> ផ្ទះ</guilabel> ព័ត៌មាន​ ដន្ត្រី​<guilabel></guilabel><guilabel>"
"</guilabel><guilabel></guilabel>."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Your Favorite Tracks</guilabel> pane lists the ten highest rated "
"tracks in your collection."
msgstr ""
"ស្លាបព្រិល​ <guilabel> បទ​សណព្វ​របស់​អ្នក  </guilabel> "
"រាយ​បញ្ជីបង់លេខបទដែល​ខ្ពស់ជាង​គេ​ចំនួន​ដប់​នៅ​ក្នុង​សម្រាំង​របស់​អ្នក​ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Your Newest Tracks</guilabel> pane lists the five most recently "
"added tracks in your collection."
msgstr ""
"ស្លាបព្រិល​<guilabel>បទ​​ថ្មី​បំផុត​របស់អ្នក</guilabel>"
"រាយ​បញ្ជី​បទ​ដែល​បាន​បន្ថែម​បច្ចុប្បន្ន​\n"
"ចំនួន​ប្រាំ​ក្នុង​សម្រាំង​របស់អ្នក ។​"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Least Listened Songs</guilabel> pane lists the five least "
"listened to tracks in your collection. These are tracks that were once played, "
"but have not been played in a while."
msgstr ""
"យ៉ាងហោចណាស់​ក៏​មាន​ស្លាបព្រិល​<guilabel>​បញ្ជី​បទចម្រៀង​​</guilabel> "
"ដែល​បានស្តាប់​បទ​ចំនួន​ប្រាំ​\n"
"ក្នុង​សម្រាំង​របស់​អ្នក ។ មាន​បទជាច្រើន​ដែល​យើង​បាន​ចាក់​ម្តងមួយៗ​ "
"ប៉ុន្តែ​មិន​មែនមិន​ត្រូវ​បានចាក់​ឥឡូវ​ទេ​។​"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:113
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking an item in any of these panes will begin playback of the track."
msgstr "បទ​."

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Current Track Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:121
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Current Track</guilabel> Tab offers information about the "
"currently playing track, and it's artist and album."
msgstr "<guilabel></guilabel> ព័ត៌មាន​ បទ​ សិល្បករ​ អាល់ប៊ុម​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:123
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first pane in this tab is for information about the track. The title of the "
"pane lists the track name, artist name, and album. Inside the pane you will "
"find it shows the album cover image for the track. Next to the image you will "
"find a <ulink url=\"http://www.musicbrainz.org/\">MusicBrainz</ulink> "
"icon. <inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"musicbrainz.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> Click this icon to do a "
"MusicBrainz look-up for the track."
msgstr ""
"ព័ត៌មាន​ បទ​ ចំណង​ជើង​ បទ​ សិល្បករ​ អាល់ប៊ុម​ អាល់ប៊ុម​ បទ​<ulink "
"url=\"http://www.musicbrainz.org/\"></ulink><inlinemediaobject><imageobject>"
"<imagedata fileref=\"musicbrainz.png\" format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject>"
"</inlinemediaobject> បទ​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:125
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below the MusicBrainz icon there is more information about you current track. "
"Here you will find the total number of times the track has been played, the "
"track's current core, and when the track was First and Last played."
msgstr "ព័ត៌មាន​ បទ​ បទ​ បទ​ បទ​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:127
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To display album cover images in the Context Browser you must have the album "
"cover image in the same directory as the track you are listening to. Supported "
"file formats are .jpg, .jpeg, .gif, and .png. The images can be named anything, "
"but images with the word <quote>front</quote> in the filename will be used with "
"preference. The Context Browser will also use cover images saved from the album "
"cover downloader, or images embedded in ID3v2 tags."
msgstr "អាល់ប៊ុម​ អាល់ប៊ុម​ បទ​<quote></quote> អាល់ប៊ុម​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:129
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next pane, <guilabel>Suggested Songs</guilabel>, lists multiple tracks for "
"suggested listening. Click on any of the listed tracks to begin playback of the "
"track."
msgstr "បន្ទាប់​<guilabel></guilabel> បទ​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:131
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below <guilabel>Suggested Songs</guilabel> is the <guilabel>"
"Favorite Tracks By Artist</guilabel>. This pane lists the five highest rated "
"tracks by the current track's artist."
msgstr "<guilabel></guilabel><guilabel> អ្នក​ចម្រៀង​</guilabel> បទ​ សិល្បករ​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:133
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The last pane, <guilabel>Albums By Artists</guilabel>"
", lists all of the albums by the current track's artists that are in your "
"collection. Clicking on any of the albums in this pane will expand the album to "
"show the album's content."
msgstr "<guilabel></guilabel> បទ​ អាល់ប៊ុម​ អាល់ប៊ុម​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:135
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can click on tracks in any of the panes to begin playback of the track. You "
"can also right click albums and tracks for a pop-up menu to choose several ways "
"to play or enqueue the track or album."
msgstr "បទ​ ចាក់​ បទ​ អាល់ប៊ុម​."

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Lyrics Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:143
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Lyrics</guilabel> Tab has a single pane that is used to display "
"the lyrics to the currently playing track if they are available."
msgstr "<guilabel></guilabel> អត្ថបទ​ចម្រៀង​ បទ​."

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Wiki Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "This tab is not yet documented."
msgstr "This tab is not yet documented."

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "Collection Browser"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: using.docbook:163
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "Collection Browser Screenshot"
msgstr "រូបថត​អេក្រង់​កម្មវិធីរុករក​សម្រាំង​ "

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:169
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Collection Browser is used to view your audio collection in a Tree View. In "
"order to use the Collection Browser, you must setup the directories to use for "
"your collection. Clicking the <guibutton>Configure Folders..</guibutton> "
"button in the Collection Browser toolbar will start a dialog for adding "
"directories to your collection."
msgstr "អូឌីយ៉ូ​<guibutton></guibutton>."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you enabled the <guilabel>Watch folders for changes</guilabel> "
"option in the <guilabel>Configure Collection</guilabel> "
"dialog you may notice that changes may not be updated instantly. This is "
"because the normal behavior of the Collection Browser is to update "
"automatically every 30 seconds."
msgstr ""
"បើ​ជម្រើស​​<guilabel>ឃ្លាំមើល​ការផ្លាស់ប្តូរ​ថត​</guilabel>"
"បាន​បើកក្នុង​ប្រអប់​<guilabel>កំណត់រចនាសម្ព័ន្ធ​សម្រាំង​</guilabel>"
"អ្នកត្រូវ​​សម្គាល់​ថា​ការផ្លាស់ប្តូរ​មិនត្រូវ​បាន​ធ្វើ​ឲ្យ​ទាន់សម័យ​ភ្លាមៗ​ទេ​ "
"។ \n"
"នេះ​ក៏​ព្រោះ​តែឥរិយាបទ​ធម្មតា​នៃ​កម្មវិធី​រុករក​សម្រាំង​បាន​ធ្វើ​ឲ្យ​ទាន់សម័យ​រា"
"ល់​៣០វិនាទីម្តង​​ដោយ\n"
"​ស្វ័យប្រវត្តិ​​។"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:173
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once your directories have been scanned, you will see your collection in a tree "
"view. The tree view is organized by <guimenuitem>First</guimenuitem>"
", <guimenuitem>Second</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Third</guimenuitem> "
"Levels. The Levels can represent the tracks Album, Artist, Genre, or Year. "
"Selecting the <guimenuitem>First</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>"
"Second</guimenuitem>, or <guimenuitem>Third</guimenuitem> "
"Level entries in the <guimenuitem>Tag Filter</guimenuitem> "
"menu will allow to set what the branches represent."
msgstr ""
"<guimenuitem></guimenuitem><guimenuitem></guimenuitem><guimenuitem>"
"</guimenuitem> អាល់ប៊ុម​ អ្នក​ចម្រៀង​ ចង្វាក់​ ឆ្នាំ​<guimenuitem></guimenuitem>"
"<guimenuitem></guimenuitem><guimenuitem></guimenuitem><guimenuitem>"
"</guimenuitem>."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:175
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Collection Browser also features a Flat View. You can choose the Flat View "
"by clicking the <guibutton>Flat View</guibutton> button in the Collection "
"Browser toolbar. In the Flat View your collection will first appear to be "
"empty. You can now start entering text into the search text box. After three or "
"more characters are entered you will begin to see the results in the Flat View. "
"You can begin another search by clicking the <guibutton>Clear Filter</guibutton> "
"button next to the text box, and then enter more text in the text box."
msgstr ""
"<guibutton></guibutton> អត្ថបទ​ អត្ថបទ​<guibutton></guibutton> "
"បន្ទាប់​ អត្ថបទ​ អត្ថបទ​ អត្ថបទ​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:177
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the top of the Collection Browser is a search bar for searching your "
"collection. The Collection Browser will show only the items that contain the "
"search string you type in the text box. Once you are done searching, you can "
"click the clear button to clear the search field."
msgstr "អត្ថបទ​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:179
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Collection Browser also supports downloading of album cover images. To "
"download an album cover you can simply right click an item in the Collection "
"Browser and select <guimenuitem>Fetch Cover Images</guimenuitem>"
". The cover downloader will open a window to display the downloaded image "
"allowing you to save the image or perform a new search with a more specific "
"search string."
msgstr "អាល់ប៊ុម​ អាល់ប៊ុម​<guimenuitem></guimenuitem>."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:181
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Included with the cover downloader is an <link linkend=\"cover-manager\">"
"Album Cover Manager</link>. You can launch the Cover Manager by selecting "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Actions</guimenu><guimenuitem>Cover Manager</guimenuitem>"
"</menuchoice>."
msgstr ""
"<link linkend=\"cover-manager\"> អាល់ប៊ុម​</link><menuchoice><guimenu></guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem></guimenuitem></menuchoice>."

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "Playlist Browser"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: using.docbook:189
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "Playlist Browser Screenshot"
msgstr "រូបថត​អេក្រង់​កម្មវិធីរុករក​បញ្ជីចាក់ "

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Playlist Browser is used for easy handling of your multiple playlists. The "
"Playlist Browser also features built in smart playlists making it the most "
"clever playlist browser around."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:197
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Playlist Browser is divided into two sections, Playlists and Smart "
"Playlists. The Playlists sections is for your own custom playlists. You can "
"view the contents of your playlists in a list view by clicking the <quote>"
"+</quote> symbol found next to each of the listed playlists. When you view a "
"playlist in the list view new items can be added to the playlist by dragging "
"and dropping them into the view. When you have found a playlist that you would "
"like to load, you can double click the playlist, or press the <keycap>"
"Space Bar</keycap> to have &amarok; load it. The other Playlist Browser "
"keyboard shortcuts can be found in the <link linkend=\"keybd-shortcuts\">"
"Keyboard Shortcuts section</link>."
msgstr ""
"<quote></quote> បន្ទាប់​<keycap> ចន្លោះ​</keycap>&amarok;<link "
"linkend=\"keybd-shortcuts\"> ផ្លូវកាត់​</link>."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you save a new playlist from the Playlist Window it is automatically added "
"to the Playlist section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The bottom section of the Playlist Browser is the Smart Playlists. The Smart "
"Playlists use &amarok;'s built in data base to compile some useful playlists on "
"the fly. The Smart Playlists include the following."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All Collection: a playlist with all the tracks that are in your configured "
"collection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Favorite Tracks: multiple playlists of the fifteen highest rated tracks in a "
"listview by artitst."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most Played: multiple playlists of the fifteen most played tracks in a listview "
"by artitst."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Newest Tracks: multiple playlists of the fifteen most recently added tracks in "
"a listview by artitst."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Last Played: a playlist of the fifteen most recently played tracks in your "
"collection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Never Played: a playlist of the tracks in your collection which have never been "
"played before."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:215
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "Genres: multiple playlists in a listview ordered by genre."
msgstr "ចង្វាក់​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"User defined smart playlists are also possible. Clicking the <guibutton>"
"Create Smart-Playlist</guibutton> button will open a dialog to configure a "
"smart playlist to fit your criteria."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "Media Device Browser"
msgstr "Media Device Browser"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: using.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Media Device Browser Screenshot"
msgstr "Media Device Browser Screenshot"

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:232
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Media Device panel is used for connecting your iPod, to &amarok;. To use "
"your iPod with the Media Device browser you must have your iPod mounted at "
"/mnt/ipod before starting &amarok;. Once you have started &amarok; you will "
"find the tracks on your iPod listed by artist in a listview at the top of the "
"browser."
msgstr "&amarok;&amarok;&amarok; សិល្បករ​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:234
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add tracks to your iPod, drag the tracks you want to add from the playlist "
"and drop them on the Artist listview. After you are done adding tracks to the "
"list click the <guibutton>Transfer</guibutton> button to upload them to your "
"iPod. After the transfer has completed, close &amarok; and unmount your iPod."
msgstr "អ្នក​ចម្រៀង​<guibutton></guibutton>&amarok;."

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Browser"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: using.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Browser Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:248
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The File Browser panel is like a mini konqueror embedded into the playlist. You "
"can use the File Browser panel to browse your entire filesystem for audio files "
"to add to the playlist. At the top of the File Browser you will find a toolbar "
"with navigation buttons for moving Up, Back, and Forward through your "
"filesystem. The tool bar also offers a Home, Reload, Short view and Detailed "
"view buttons, it also features a Bookmarks button for creating bookmarks of "
"your favorite filesystem areas."
msgstr "អូឌីយ៉ូ​ ត្រឡប់​ បញ្ចូន​បន្ត​ ផ្ទះ ផ្ទុក​ឡើង​វិញ ."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below the toolbar is a handy search bar for searching by file name. You will "
"find the search bar useful for directories with many files as it searches as "
"you type leaving only the relevant file names in the view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:252
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the File Browser is an address bar for accessing your music "
"from any URL that you type. For instance typing <filename class=\"directory\">"
"tar:/home/mike/music.tar.gz</filename> into the address bar and pressing "
"<keycap>Enter</keycap> on your keyboard will allow you to access the files "
"inside the music tar ball. Now you can drag the audio from the tar ball and "
"drop it into the playlist."
msgstr ""
"ដន្ត្រី​<filename class=\"directory\"> ដន្ត្រី​</filename><keycap></keycap> "
"ដន្ត្រី​ អូឌីយ៉ូ​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When playlist grows larger than one screenful, it becomes hard to append files "
"by simply dropping them. Holding <keycap>Shift</keycap> "
"key on keyboard while dropping may help in this case: the files will be "
"appended at the end of playlist rather than inserted at current drop position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: using.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Playlist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: using.docbook:265
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid "Playlist Screenshot"
msgstr "រូបថត​អេក្រង់​បញ្ជីចាក់ "

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:273
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Playlist holds all the tracks you have en-queued for playing. You can "
"change the sequence by dragging items around with the mouse, and dropping them "
"in the desired position. Above the Playlist you see a Text Box, where you can "
"enter a filter string. As soon as you enter a letter there, the Playlist will "
"be redisplayed, showing only entries containing the entered characters. To stop "
"the filtering, simply press <keycap>Backspace</keycap>"
", until the filter is empty."
msgstr "អត្ថបទ​ បញ្ឈប់​<keycap> លុប​ថយ​ក្រោម​</keycap>."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced, Google-esque syntax is also available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, when you enter terms separated by spaces, it will search for items "
"containing all of them. For example: one two three, will search for anything "
"that contains one, two, and three."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"However, you can put OR between terms to search for items that contain either, "
"like this: one OR two OR three. That way, it will search for items that contain "
"either one, or two, or three (or a combination of them)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also use quotes to search for terms with spaces in them: \"Mike "
"Oldfield\". That will search for items that contain Mike Oldfield, but not, for "
"example, ones that contain Mike J. Oldfield."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:286
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, it searches in all the columns of the playlist that are currently "
"visible. However, you can use column:term to specify the column to search in: "
"title:amarok (this can also be a column that isn't visible). This way, it will "
"only search for items that have the word amarok in the title, and not, for "
"example, in the album."
msgstr "ចំណង​ជើង​ ចំណង​ជើង​ អាល់ប៊ុម​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:289
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When specifying a specific column to search in, you can also search for items "
"less than or greater than a term, for example: score:>"
"50, which will search for items with a score greater than 50."
msgstr "ពិន្ទុ​ ពិន្ទុ​."

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To specify a term you don't want the items to match, you can put a minus (-) "
"sign before them: -thing, to search for anything that doesn't contain thing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using.docbook:293
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can combine the above at will, for example: \"Mike Oldfield\" OR score:>"
"50 -comment:bad. That will search for anything that either contains Mike "
"Oldfield or has a score greater than 50, but excludes items where the comment "
"contains \"bad\"."
msgstr "ពិន្ទុ​ សេចក្តីអធិប្បាយ​ ពិន្ទុ​ សេចក្តីអធិប្បាយ​."

